From eacf43b98c63d51bcb4b8c16514f59235fc46739 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jason chien <3936511+jason5545@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:35:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] steamac: share textures through host memory without Win32
 handle export

CrossOver on macOS (KosmicKrisp behind CrossOver 27 Wine) exposes no
VK_KHR_external_memory_win32 to applications, but does expose
VK_EXT_external_memory_host. On such devices, committed textures with
D3D12_HEAP_FLAG_SHARED now live in a pagefile-backed section: a header
at offset 0 and a LINEAR image from 64 KiB on, imported with
VK_EXT_external_memory_host. CreateSharedHandle returns a new handle to
the section; OpenSharedHandle accepts section handles (NT or the KMT
handles DXVK hands out). DXVK (jason5545/dxvk-steamac,
src/dxvk/dxvk_shared_section.h) uses the same layout.

- Only active on devices without VK_KHR_external_memory_win32;
  elsewhere nothing changes. Placed resources in shared heaps and
  shared buffers keep their old behavior; CreateSharedHandle on them
  fails cleanly instead of calling missing Win32 export functions.
- Shared textures that host memory cannot back (mips, arrays, MSAA,
  multi-planar, depth-stencil, unsupported LINEAR usage) fail to create
  instead of being created unshared.
- Imported shared memory skips zero-initialization, and host pointer
  imports with VKD3D_ALLOCATION_FLAG_NO_FALLBACK no longer fall back to
  an unshared allocation.
- The section is unmapped in d3d12_resource_destroy after the memory.
- STEAMAC_NO_HOST_SHARING=1 disables the path.
---
 libs/vkd3d/device.c        |  47 +++++
 libs/vkd3d/hostshare.c     | 377 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libs/vkd3d/memory.c        |  14 +-
 libs/vkd3d/meson.build     |   2 +-
 libs/vkd3d/resource.c      |  54 +++++-
 libs/vkd3d/vkd3d_private.h |  72 +++++++
 6 files changed, 559 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libs/vkd3d/hostshare.c

